$AB \parallel CD$ means line $AB$ is **parallel** to line $CD$, staying the same distance away.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (-2.4,1.1) -- (2.4,1.1);
\node[left] at (-2.4,1.1) {$A$};
\node[right] at (2.4,1.1) {$B$};
\draw (-2.4,-1.1) -- (2.4,-1.1);
\node[left] at (-2.4,-1.1) {$C$};
\node[right] at (2.4,-1.1) {$D$};
\draw[->] (-0.35,1.1) -- (0.35,1.1);
\draw[->] (-0.35,-1.1) -- (0.35,-1.1);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$EF \perp GH$ means line $EF$ is **perpendicular** to line $GH$, meeting it at $90^{\circ}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (X) at (0,0);
\coordinate (E) at (-2.2,0);
\coordinate (F) at (2.2,0);
\coordinate (G) at (0,-1.9);
\coordinate (H) at (0,1.9);
\draw (E) -- (F);
\draw (G) -- (H);
\coordinate (p) at ($(X)!0.32cm!(F)$);
\coordinate (q) at ($(X)!0.32cm!(H)$);
\draw (p) -- ($(p)+(q)-(X)$) -- (q);
\node[left] at (E) {$E$};
\node[right] at (F) {$F$};
\node[below] at (G) {$G$};
\node[above] at (H) {$H$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Matching arrowhead marks identify parallel lines, and a different number of arrowheads identifies a different parallel set.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (3.6,0);
\coordinate (R) at (4.6,2.4);
\coordinate (S) at (1.0,2.4);
\draw (P) -- (Q);
\draw (S) -- (R);
\draw (P) -- (S);
\draw (Q) -- (R);
\node[below left] at (P) {$P$};
\node[below right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[above right] at (R) {$R$};
\node[above left] at (S) {$S$};
\draw[->] (1.5,0) -- (2.1,0);
\draw[->] (2.5,2.4) -- (3.1,2.4);
\draw[->] (0.2692,0.6462) -- (0.4808,1.1538);
\draw[->] (0.5192,1.2462) -- (0.7308,1.7538);
\draw[->] (3.8692,0.6462) -- (4.0808,1.1538);
\draw[->] (4.1192,1.2462) -- (4.3308,1.7538);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A **transversal** is a line that crosses two or more other lines at different points.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.8,1.3) -- (2.8,0.9) node[pos=0.93, above] {$l$};
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.8,-1.5) -- (2.8,-1.1) node[pos=0.93, below] {$m$};
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-1.5,-2.5) -- (1.7,2.5) node[pos=0.88, left] {$t$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

